---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout 
  title="Privacy Policy - Antology.ai"
  description="Privacy Policy for Antology.ai's AI-powered route optimization platform. Learn how we protect and handle your data."
>
  <!-- Navigation -->
  <nav class="fixed top-0 w-full bg-white/95 backdrop-blur-sm z-50 border-b border-gray-100">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="flex justify-between items-center h-16">
        <div class="flex items-center">
          <a href="/">
            <img src="/logo.png" alt="Antology.ai" class="h-8 w-auto" />
          </a>
        </div>
        <div class="hidden md:flex items-center space-x-8">
          <a href="/#how-it-works" class="text-gray-600 hover:text-primary transition-colors">How It Works</a>
          <a href="/#features" class="text-gray-600 hover:text-primary transition-colors">Features</a>
          <a href="/#why-antology" class="text-gray-600 hover:text-primary transition-colors">Why Antology</a>
          <a href="/#optimize-deliveries" class="text-gray-600 hover:text-primary transition-colors">Contact Us</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </nav>

  <!-- Privacy Policy Content -->
  <main class="pt-24 pb-16">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none">
        <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-8">Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="text-gray-600 mb-8">Last Updated: October 01, 2025</p>

        <section class="mb-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-4">1. Introduction</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            This Privacy Policy describes how Antology ("we," "our," or "us") collects, uses, and shares information when you use our route optimization services, websites, applications, and related software (collectively, the "Service").
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            By using Antology, you consent to the collection and use of your information as described in this Privacy Policy.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="mb-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-4">2. Updates to the Privacy Policy</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time by posting an updated version on our website and revising the "Last Updated" date at the top of this page.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            Continued use of the Service after such updates constitutes your acceptance of the revised Privacy Policy.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            If we make material changes, we will provide notice as required by applicable law.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="mb-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-4">3. Information We Collect</h2>

          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-3 mt-6">a) Account Information</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            We collect your name, company name, email address, phone number, and login credentials when you create an account or communicate with us.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-3 mt-6">b) Customer Data</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            When you use Antology, you may provide data such as delivery addresses, orders, vehicle details, agent information, time windows, and other logistics-related data ("Customer Data"). You retain ownership of all Customer Data you upload or submit to Antology.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-3 mt-6">c) Usage Data</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            We automatically collect information about how you use Antology, including your IP address, browser type, device identifiers, operating system, pages viewed, actions performed, and access times. This helps us improve the performance, security, and reliability of the Service.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-3 mt-6">d) Location Data</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            To provide accurate routing and optimization, we may collect and process geographic location data from your devices, such as GPS coordinates or mapped addresses, when enabled by you or your organization.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-3 mt-6">e) Communications</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            We may collect information from your communications with our support, sales, or operations teams, including messages, feedback, and inquiries.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="mb-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-4">4. How We Use Information</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">We use the information we collect for the following purposes:</p>
          <ul class="list-none text-gray-700 mb-4">
            <li class="mb-2">a) To provide, maintain, and improve our route optimization and logistics planning services.</li>
            <li class="mb-2">b) To process Customer Data and generate optimized routes, analytics, and recommendations.</li>
            <li class="mb-2">c) To communicate with you regarding your account, updates, or support.</li>
            <li class="mb-2">d) To enhance security and prevent fraudulent or unauthorized access.</li>
            <li class="mb-2">e) To analyze usage trends, improve product performance, and develop new features.</li>
            <li class="mb-2">f) To comply with applicable laws, regulations, and contractual obligations.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="mb-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-4">5. Data Ownership and Retention</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            You own all Customer Data that you provide to Antology. We process it only to deliver our Services.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            We may retain Customer Data and related records for as long as your account is active or as necessary to provide the Service, resolve disputes, comply with legal obligations, or enforce our agreements. Upon termination, data may be deleted or anonymized in accordance with our Data Retention Policy.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="mb-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-4">6. Sharing of Information</h2>

          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-3 mt-6">a) With Service Providers and Subprocessors</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            We may share information with trusted third parties who perform services such as cloud hosting, analytics, or customer support on our behalf. These subprocessors are bound by confidentiality and data protection agreements consistent with this Privacy Policy.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-3 mt-6">b) With Third-Party Integrations</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            If you choose to connect Antology with third-party systems (e.g., ERP, dispatch, or CRM tools), we will share necessary data to enable such integrations. You control which integrations are active.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-3 mt-6">c) For Legal or Regulatory Reasons</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            We may disclose information if required by law or when we believe disclosure is necessary to protect our rights, investigate fraud, or respond to lawful requests by public authorities.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="mb-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-4">7. Security</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            We implement reasonable administrative, technical, and physical safeguards to protect your data against unauthorized access, loss, misuse, or alteration. However, no system can guarantee complete security.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="mb-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-4">8. International Data Transfers</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            Your information may be transferred to and processed in countries other than your own. These countries may have different data protection laws, but we ensure that adequate safeguards are in place as required by applicable regulations.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="mb-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-4">9. Your Rights and Choices</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">Depending on your jurisdiction, you may have the right to:</p>
          <ul class="list-none text-gray-700 mb-4">
            <li class="mb-2">Access and obtain a copy of your personal data.</li>
            <li class="mb-2">Request correction or deletion of your data.</li>
            <li class="mb-2">Restrict or object to data processing.</li>
            <li class="mb-2">Withdraw consent at any time where processing is based on consent.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="mb-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-4">10. Cookies and Tracking Technologies</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            We use cookies, pixels, and similar technologies to understand usage patterns, enhance functionality, and improve your experience. You can manage cookie preferences through your browser settings.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="mb-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-4">11. Children's Privacy</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            Antology is not intended for use by individuals under 18 years of age. We do not knowingly collect personal data from minors.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>